MDL101, K15, F1: a UTF-8 byte order mark makes the first line "\ufeff[client]",
which GLib rejects, so mydumper ignores the whole file and exits 0 with
users.email in plaintext. The linter also claims (F12) that the connection
still works through [client]: the MySQL client library must then skip the BOM.
The BOM is also text before '[' on the first line, so the pre-processor does
not reset its state after it (P1, MDL112).
-- scenario --
tool: mydumper
versions: >= v0.19.1-1
args: --defaults-file /work/defaults.cnf --database app
lint: MDL101, MDL112, MDL405
expect config-loaded: false
expect exit: 0
expect connected: true
expect column app.users.email: plaintext
-- defaults.cnf.esc --
\xef\xbb\xbf[client]\nhost=mysql\nuser=e2e\npassword=e2e-password\n\n[mydumper]\nthreads=2\n\n[`app`.`users`]\n`email`=random_string\n
